                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A cinematic, striking, and unforgettable narrative experience. \nVirginia is a fascinating interactive thriller that plays out like a surreal 90s TV drama in the vein of Twin Peaks. Playing as an FBI agent investigating a missing person case, the game's boldest and most unique aspect is its decision to tell the entire story without a single word of dialogue or text, relying purely on brilliant cinematic editing and a phenomenal orchestral soundtrack. While the gameplay is minimal—mostly a \"walking simulator\" where you move from scene to scene—the experimental storytelling and mystery keep you completely hooked. It is short, highly artistic, and open to interpretation, making it a must-play for fans of narrative-driven experiences.",
